hen the command \\"/stitch\\" is present in the message"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "7ad2cba9-a301-4960-bd2d-8498671c1fec", "name": "Get Text", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [-480, -336], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "029f4e7e-b367-4aa9-863e-e372694940fb", "name": "chatInput", "type": "string", "value": "={{ $json.message.text }}"}, {"id": "398c1d7f-0c90-4af6-a414-d4d1968855b9", "name": "sessionId", "type": "number", "value": "={{ $json.message.from.id }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "fa76c04c-1624-4c8a-a0cd-80b0660ac2f4", "name": "Send a text message", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram", "position": [1392, -512], "webhookId": "160197ce-5576-4437-8ee6-11796f3ce192", "parameters": {"text": "={{ $json.text }}", "chatId": "={{ $('Get Message').item.json.message.from.id }}", "additionalFields": {"parse_mode": "HTML"}}, "credentials": {"telegramApi": {"id": "XP2SJ3wLc8EY82QZ", "name": "Telegram API"}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "725d1d2f-fabd-4c6e-8a84-c0619412e662", "name": "Google Gemini Chat Model1", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini", "position": [1056, -320], "parameters": {"options": {}}, "credentials": {"googlePalmApi": {"id": "11a68a950433485d", "name": "Dummy googlePalmApi"}}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "dd7b7f1c-c2d2-4d34-958c-ade116e05752", "name": "Google Stitch Agent", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent", "position": [256, -336], "parameters": {"options": {"systemMessage": "=You are an AI agent with access to the Google Stitch MCP tool.\\nYour task is to intelligently use Stitch to support design, UI generation, and product prototyping workflows.\\n\\nBefore taking any action, do the following:\\n\\nInspect and enumerate all available functions exposed by the Google Stitch MCP tool, including (but not limited to):\\n\\nUI or layout generation\\n\\nScreen or component creation\\n\\nDesign system or style token handling\\n\\nUX flow generation\\n\\nWireframe or mockup synthesis\\n\\nAny transformation, export, or validation capabilities\\n\\nEvaluate which function or combination of functions best fits the user\\u2019s request, considering:\\n\\nLevel of fidelity (wireframe vs high-fidelity UI)\\n\\nPlatform target (web, mobile, desktop)\\n\\nDesign intent (exploration, iteration, production-ready)\\n\\nInput constraints (text-only prompt, structured data, existing components)\\n\\nIf the request is ambiguous or underspecified, make reasonable assumptions and clearly state them before calling the tool.\\n\\nCall the Google Stitch MCP tool using the most appropriate function(s) and provide:\\n\\nClear, structured inputs\\n\\nDescriptive naming for screens, components, and flows\\n\\nConsistent design intent across outputs\\n\\nAfter the tool call:\\n\\nSummarize what was generated\\n\\nExplain which Stitch functions were used and why\\n\\nSuggest possible follow-up actions or refinements using other available Stitch capabilities\\n\\nConstraints\\n\\nDo not hallucinate Stitch features that are not exposed by the MCP tool.\\n\\nPrefer modular, reusable UI and design outputs.\\n\\nOptimize for clarity, usability, and extensibility.\\n\\nAct as a design-aware AI agent: pragmatic, structured, and intentional in how you use Google Stitch.\\n\\nUse search on web tool in necessary"}}, "typeVersion": 3.1}, {"id": "37dd1c91-74f7-4fdd-8fa2-0c9d97f76766", "name": "From MD to HTML", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm", "position": [1056, -512], "parameters": {"text": "={{ $json.output }}", "batching": {}, "messages": {"messageValues": [{"message": "Convert this text from markdown to html format for telegram message.\\n\\nWithout ```html\\\\n and \\\\n```...only html for telegram.\\n\\nTelegram supports a limited set of HTML tags including <b>, <strong>, <i>, <em>, <u>, <ins>, <s>, <strike>, <code>, <pre>, and <a>. "}]}, "promptType": "define"}, "typeVersion": 1.9}, {"id": "e9e6cfa0-2340-4b8e-baa7-ac69bde3b5aa", "name": "Clean query", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [-96, -336], "parameters": {"jsCode": "for (const item of $input.all()) {\\n  const originalText = item.json.chatInput;\\n\\n  const query = originalText.replace(\\"/stitch \\", \\"\\");\\n\\n  item.json.chatInput = query;\\n  item.json.sessionId = item.json.sessionId;\\n}\\n\\nreturn $input.all();\\n"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "25a65c54-bee4-4e63-a2b7-1788427fcd77", "name": "is Telegram?", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "position": [768, -336], "parameters": {"options": {"ignoreCase": true}, "conditions": {"options": {"version": 3, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": false, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "a57cbda0-cd51-4842-9747-19b0415a96c9", "operator": {"type": "boolean", "operation": "true", "singleValue": true}, "leftValue": "={{ $('Get Message').isExecuted }}", "rightValue": ""}]}}, "typeVersion": 2.3}, {"id": "8b8a2d45-29b8-440e-ae01-ee4e8ab3a8d3", "name": "Sticky Note9", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1008, -624], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 672, "height": 452, "content": "## STEP 3- Send Response\\n\\nSet response message for Telegram and send it"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "42bbb0f3-0e2e-4bfb-8f14-4160b7b7d378", "name": "Sticky Note1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [-1024, -1104], "parameters": {"width": 704, "height": 592, "content": "## AI-powered Google Stitch Design Agent via Telegram using MCP and Gemini\\nThis workflow implements an **AI-powered design and prototyping assistant** that integrates **Telegram**, **Google Gemini**, and **Google Stitch (MCP)** to enable conversational UI generation and project management.\\n\\n### **How it works**\\n\\nThis workflow acts as a Telegram-based AI design assistant that uses Google Gemini as an LLM and Google Stitch MCP tools to manage design projects and generate UI screens from natural language. Incoming Telegram messages are authorized by user ID and filtered to only run when the `/stitch` command is used. The cleaned user query is passed to an AI agent with conversational memory, which analyzes intent and selectively calls Stitch MCP functions such as project creation, screen listing, or UI generation. The agent can also use web search when additional context is needed. Responses are converted from Markdown to Telegram-compatible HTML before being sent back to the user.\\n\\n### **Setup steps**\\n\\nConfigure Telegram access by setting your Telegram User ID in the authorization Code node and ensuring bot credentials are valid for both trigger and response nodes. Set up Google Stitch by creating an API key and configuring an HTTP Header Auth credential with `X-Goog-Api-Key`, which is shared across all Stitch MCP tool nodes. Verify credentials for the Google Gemini chat model and the Perplexity web search tool if used. After all credentials are in place, activate the workflow so the Telegram webhook is registered and the agent can respond to `/stitch` commands.\\n"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "37dcf1d8-119b-4e2b-99f9-4159ad3e5931", "name": "Sticky Note10", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [-288, -1248], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 736, "height": 736, "content": "## MY NEW YOUTUBE CHANNEL\\n\\ud83d\\udc49 [Subscribe to my new **YouTube channel**](https://youtube.com/@n3witalia). Here I\\u2019ll share videos and Shorts with practical tutorials and **FREE templates for n8n**.\\n\\n[![image](https://n3wstorage.b-cdn.net/n3witalia/youtube-n8n-cover.jpg)](https://youtube.com/@n3witalia)"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459361", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "Q2jXWo-iO_eefuMxGrDYq", "parameters": {"path": "Q2jXWo-iO_eefuMxGrDYq", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]	{"Code":{"main":[[{"node":"Search with MCP?","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Get Text":{"main":[[{"node":"Clean query","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Get screen":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"Clean query":{"main":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Get Message":{"main":[[{"node":"Code","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Get Project":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"List screen":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"is Telegram?":{"main":[[{"node":"From MD to HTML","type":"main","index":0}]]},"List projects":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"Search on web":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"Simple Memory":{"ai_memory":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_memory","index":0}]]},"Create Project":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"From MD to HTML":{"main":[[{"node":"Send a text message","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Generate Screen":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"Search with MCP?":{"main":[[{"node":"Get Text","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Google Stitch Agent":{"main":[[{"node":"is Telegram?","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Google Gemini Chat Model":{"ai_languageModel":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0}]]},"Google Gemini Chat Model1":{"ai_languageModel":[[{"node":"From MD to HTML","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0}]]},"When chat message received":{"main":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Automata Webhook":{"main":[[{"node":"Google Stitch Agent","type":"main","index":0},{"node":"Code","type":"main","index":0}]]}}	2026-10-03 17:43:45.791+00	2026-10-04 11:11:49.747+00	{"callerPolicy":"workflowsFromSameOwner","timeSavedMode":"fixed","availableInMCP":false,"executionOrder":"v1","executionTimeout":3600}	\N	{}	2efcc13b-f8f6-4c7f-b77c-a993fad0dc88	0	Q2jXWo-iO_eefuMxGrDYq	{"instanceId":"a4bfc93e975ca233ac45ed7c9227d84cf5a2329310525917adaf3312e10d5462","templateCredsSetupCompleted":true}	\N	f	5	\N	\N	[]	\N
[AUTOMATA][CODING] Send engineering daily digest to Slack with Jira, GitHub, OpenAI, and Google Shee	t	[{"id": "8b8b9beb-e001-4641-9634-be79a499e10f", "name": "Sticky Note", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [176, 80], "parameters": {"width": 480, "height": 896, "content": "## Engineering Daily Digest\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\nThis workflow runs every weekday at 9 AM, loads engineering digest settings, and collects Jira and GitHub signals in parallel. It finds recent Jira activity, stale in-progress Jira tickets, recent GitHub pull request activity, and stale pull requests without reviews, then normalizes and merges those findings. The combined data is summarized with OpenAI, formatted into Slack blocks, posted to Slack, and optionally logged to Google Sheets for velocity tracking.\\n\\n### Setup steps\\n\\n- Configure the weekday schedule trigger, including the intended timezone for the 9 AM run.\\n- Set the Config node values such as jiraBaseUrl, jiraProjectKey, staleTicketDays, staleReviewHours, repository list, Slack channel, and any sheet logging flag used by the workflow.\\n- Add Jira credentials with permission to search issues in the configured project.\\n- Add GitHub credentials or an API token with access to the repositories and pull request/search endpoints used by the workflow.\\n- Add OpenAI credentials and confirm the summarization model/prompt are appropriate for engineering digest content.\\n- Add Slack credentials with permission to post messages to the target channel.\\n- If sheet logging is enabled, add Google Sheets credentials and configure the target spreadsheet, sheet, and appended row fields.\\n\\n### Customization\\n\\nAdjust staleTicketDays, staleReviewHours, repository lists, Jira queries, the OpenAI summary prompt, Slack block formatting, and the Google Sheets logging toggle/columns to match the team’s reporting needs."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "fdcecf8e-bba4-4fff-936a-75c9bb5945d0", "name": "Sticky Note1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [736, 192], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 416, "height": 320, "content": "## Schedule and config\\n\\nStarts the workflow on weekday mornings and defines shared settings used by the Jira, GitHub, Slack, and logging branches."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "d5e40617-2d2f-467d-9636-bed6150f8e90", "name": "Sticky Note2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1472, 288], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 432, "height": 304, "content": "## Jira stale tickets\\n\\nQueries Jira for stale in-progress issues and normalizes them into a digest-friendly format."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "3c5b3384-8235-4ca3-8ebc-db6a88994d20", "name": "Sticky Note3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1296, 800], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 416, "height": 320, "content": "## Jira recent activity\\n\\nFetches Jira activity from the last 24 hours and converts the results into a consistent normalized structure."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "986896ab-2cef-424d-a2c3-4efb288d3c7a", "name": "Sticky Note4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2128, 80], "parameters": {"color": 7, "height": 336, "content": "## Merge Jira findings\\n\\nCombines the normalized recent and stale Jira result streams into one Jira digest payload."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "4fc9cda0-004d-4598-b5e3-43d16efe28dc", "name": "Sticky Note5", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1344, 1152], "parameters": {"color": 7, "height": 336, "content": "## Repository fan-out\\n\\nExpands the configured repository list so GitHub checks can run for each repository."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "debb08cb-4bd2-415c-b2d1-5ec794420ba4", "name": "Sticky Note6", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2048, 656], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 640, "height": 304, "content": "## GitHub recent activity\\n\\nRetrieves recent pull request activity from GitHub, flattens repository-level results, and normalizes them for the digest."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "e564036f-ecf8-410e-8b71-e030ec76a9bc", "name": "Sticky Note7", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1840, 1600], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 640, "height": 304, "content": "## GitHub stale reviews\\n\\nSearches GitHub for stale pull requests without reviews, flattens the API response, and normalizes the findings."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "38313b12-be69-4c21-9ff4-baf887514460", "name": "Sticky Note8", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2400, 256], "parameters": {"color": 7, "height": 368, "content": "## Merge GitHub findings\\n\\nCombines the normalized recent pull request activity with the stale review findings into a single GitHub digest stream."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "9ad1bf9c-444f-4f7a-92a8-97ebe799b7f4", "name": "Sticky Note9", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [3216, 320], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 800, "height": 656, "content": "## Summarize and format\\n\\nMerges Jira and GitHub data, generates an AI-written digest summary, parses the model output, and builds Slack message blocks."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "0415b5f3-670e-48c2-b95c-c8c048b5b205", "name": "Sticky Note10", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [4048, 624], "parameters": {"color": 7, "height": 336, "content": "## Post Slack digest\\n\\nPublishes the formatted engineering digest to the configured Slack destination."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "069015a1-0e29-4905-a848-d50dc36cbe46", "name": "Sticky Note11", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [4720, 512], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 416, "height": 528, "content": "## Optional sheet logging\\n\\nChecks whether spreadsheet logging is enabled, appends a velocity row to Google Sheets when enabled, or exits through a no-op branch when disabled."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "2be2f2bb-fee5-4f53-8f1c-98c9460ead84", "name": "When Weekday 9AM", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger", "position": [784, 352], "parameters": {"rule": {"interval": [{"field": "cronExpression", "expression": "0 9 * * 1-5"}]}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "98779315-d2dd-4b36-8b33-4b1db9a343cd", "name": "Set Config Fields", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "notes": "Single source of truth for everything the digest needs to run. Edit values here, nowhere else.", "position": [1008, 352], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "cfg-1", "name": "jiraBaseUrl", "type": "string", "value": "https://intuz.atlassian.net"}, {"id": "cfg-2", "name": "jiraProjectKey", "type": "string", "value": "PTN"}, {"id": "cfg-3", "name": "staleTicketDays", "type": "number", "value": 3}, {"id": "cfg-4", "name": "staleReviewHours", "type": "number", "value": 48}, {"id": "cfg-5", "name": "repos", "type": "array", "value": "=[{\\"owner\\": \\"IntuzDiyaB\\", \\"name\\": \\"Testing-n8n\\"}]"}, {"id": "cfg-6", "name": "slackChannel", "type": "string", "value": "#eng-daily-digest"}, {"id": "cfg-7", "name": "userMap", "type": "object", "value": "={ \\"jira-account-id-example\\": \\"U0123ABC\\", \\"github-login-example\\": \\"U0456DEF\\" }"}, {"id": "cfg-8", "name": "sheetEnabled", "type": "boolean", "value": true}, {"id": "cfg-9", "name": "sheetId", "type": "string", "value": "your-google-sheet-id"}, {"id": "cfg-10", "name": "sheetTabName", "type": "string", "value": "Velocity"}, {"id": "cfg-11", "name": "openAiModel", "type": "string", "value": "gpt-4o-mini"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "544a162b-2a40-4bac-b279-28a9dc369303", "name": "Fetch Jira Recent Activity", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.jira", "notes": "JQL: project = {jiraProjectKey} AND updated >= -1d ORDER BY updated DESC", "position": [1344, 960], "parameters": {"options": {"jql": "=project = {{ $json.jiraProjectKey }} AND updated >= -1d ORDER BY updated DESC"}, "operation": "getAll", "returnAll": true}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "1913330c-0dfa-4ce1-a3a9-a807c280a812", "name": "Fetch Jira Stale Tasks", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.jira", "notes": "JQL: project = {jiraProjectKey} AND status = \\"In Progress\\" AND updated <= -{staleTicketDays}d ORDER BY updated ASC", "position": [1520, 416], "parameters": {"options": {"jql": "=project = {{ $json.jiraProjectKey }} AND status = \\"In Progress\\" AND updated <= -{{ $json.staleTicketDays }}d ORDER BY updated ASC"}, "operation": "getAll", "returnAll": true}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "0e510306-abb4-481b-954a-a120a2700d4c", "name": "Normalize Jira Recent Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1568, 960], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const baseUrl = $('Set Config Fields').item.json.jiraBaseUrl;\\nconst issues = $input.all().map(item => {\\n  const issue = item.json;\\n  return {\\n    key: issue.key,\\n    summary: issue.fields?.summary,\\n    status: issue.fields?.status?.name,\\n    assignee: issue.fields?.assignee?.displayName || 'Unassigned',\\n    assigneeAccountId: issue.fields?.assignee?.accountId || null,\\n    updated: issue.fields?.updated,\\n    url: `${baseUrl}/browse/${issue.key}`\\n  };\\n});\\nreturn [{ json: { recentIssues: issues } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "2e8da8ef-48a6-4412-9387-250809ff912f", "name": "Normalize Jira Stale Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1760, 416], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const baseUrl = $('Set Config Fields').item.json.jiraBaseUrl;\\nconst now = Date.now();\\nconst issues = $input.all().map(item => {\\n  const issue = item.json;\\n  const updated = new Date(issue.fields?.updated).getTime();\\n  const daysStale = Math.floor((now - updated) / 86400000);\\n  return {\\n    key: issue.key,\\n    summary: issue.fields?.summary,\\n    status: issue.fields?.status?.name,\\n    assignee: issue.fields?.assignee?.displayName || 'Unassigned',\\n    assigneeAccountId: issue.fields?.assignee?.accountId || null,\\n    updated: issue.fields?.updated,\\n    daysStale,\\n    url: `${baseUrl}/browse/${issue.key}`\\n  };\\n});\\nreturn [{ json: { staleIssues: issues } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "4e6dfe1e-639f-4b54-8661-401ed83e99e7", "name": "Merge Jira Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [2176, 256], "parameters": {"mode": "combine", "options": {"includeUnpaired": true}, "combineBy": "combineByPosition"}, "typeVersion": 3}, {"id": "bf1ef184-71c7-469b-9723-8c223378165e", "name": "Split Repository List", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "notes": "Fans out Config.repos into one item per repo so the GitHub HTTP Request nodes run once per repo automatically.", "position": [1392, 1328], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const config = $json;\\nconst sinceISO = new Date(Date.now() - 24*60*60*1000).toISOString();\\nconst staleHours = config.staleReviewHours || 48;\\nconst staleDateISO = new Date(Date.now() - staleHours*60*60*1000).toISOString().split('T')[0];\\nreturn (config.repos || []).map(repo => ({\\n  json: {\\n    owner: repo.owner,\\n    name: repo.name,\\n    fullName: `${repo.owner}/${repo.name}`,\\n    sinceISO,\\n    staleDateISO\\n  }\\n}));"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "3e861fab-fb55-47b0-91ff-7a85c1d7b91b", "name": "Fetch Stale GitHub PRs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "notes": "GET /search/issues?q=repo:{owner}/{name}+is:pr+is:open+review:none — the review:none qualifier is the cheap way to find PRs nobody has reviewed, no per-PR calls needed.", "position": [1888, 1728], "parameters": {"url": "https://api.github.com/search/issues", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "q", "value": "=repo:{{ $json.fullName }} is:pr is:open review:none"}, {"name": "per_page", "value": "50"}]}, "nodeCredentialType": "githubApi"}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "a60d9b50-b3ec-400e-880f-9f43133f24e7", "name": "Flatten GitHub PR Activity", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2320, 784], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const results = [];\\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\\n  const body = item.json;\\n  if (Array.isArray(body)) {\\n    for (const pr of body) {\\n      if (pr && pr.number != null) results.push({ json: pr });\\n    }\\n  } else if (body && body.number != null) {\\n    results.push({ json: body });\\n  }\\n}\\nreturn results.length ? results : [{ json: { number: null } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "782da25f-dcd4-4ba8-98da-54fa6a98711e", "name": "Flatten GitHub Stale PRs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2112, 1728], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const results = [];\\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\\n  const body = item.json;\\n  const list = Array.isArray(body?.items) ? body.items : [];\\n  for (const issue of list) {\\n    if (issue && issue.number != null) results.push({ json: issue });\\n  }\\n}\\nreturn results.length ? results : [{ json: { number: null } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "52a1284b-a39f-4669-9e58-094c12737d79", "name": "Normalize GitHub Recent Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2544, 784], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const now = Date.now();\\nconst cutoff = now - 24*60*60*1000;\\nconst prs = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(pr => pr && pr.number != null);\\nconst opened = [], merged = [], closed = [];\\nfor (const pr of prs) {\\n  const createdAt = new Date(pr.created_at).getTime();\\n  const mergedAt = pr.merged_at ? new Date(pr.merged_at).getTime() : null;\\n  const closedAt = pr.closed_at ? new Date(pr.closed_at).getTime() : null;\\n  const entry = {\\n    number: pr.number,\\n    title: pr.title,\\n    author: pr.user?.login,\\n    url: pr.html_url,\\n    repo: pr.base?.repo?.full_name\\n  };\\n  if (createdAt >= cutoff) opened.push(entry);\\n  if (mergedAt && mergedAt >= cutoff) merged.push(entry);\\n  if (closedAt && !mergedAt && closedAt >= cutoff) closed.push(entry);\\n}\\nreturn [{ json: { prsOpened: opened, prsMerged: merged, prsClosed: closed } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "d5083785-305e-490b-8e09-d201209c5d6a", "name": "Normalize GitHub Stale Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2336, 1728], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const staleReviewHours = $('Set Config Fields').item.json.staleReviewHours || 48;\\nconst cutoffMs = staleReviewHours * 60 * 60 * 1000;\\nconst now = Date.now();\\nconst prs = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(pr => pr && pr.number != null);\\nconst stale = prs\\n  .filter(pr => (now - new Date(pr.created_at).getTime()) > cutoffMs)\\n  .map(pr => ({\\n    number: pr.number,\\n    title: pr.title,\\n    author: pr.user?.login,\\n    url: pr.html_url,\\n    repo: (pr.repository_url || '').split('/repos/')[1],\\n    hoursOpen: Math.floor((now - new Date(pr.created_at).getTime()) / 3600000)\\n  }));\\nreturn [{ json: { prsAwaitingReview: stale } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "63a8011d-5aba-4e13-831f-cf1886cc6cf9", "name": "Merge GitHub Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [2448, 464], "parameters": {"mode": "combine", "options": {"includeUnpaired": true}, "combineBy": "combineByPosition"}, "typeVersion": 3}, {"id": "4293cf7f-7a93-4636-80e1-6bf93c63841a", "name": "Merge Overall Digest", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [3264, 448], "parameters": {"mode": "combine", "options": {"includeUnpaired": true}, "combineBy": "combineByPosition"}, "typeVersion": 3}, {"id": "81673de3-b001-4b65-a7da-f543ec8ee25a", "name": "Parse LLM Summary", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [3648, 800], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const response = $json;\\nconst digest = $('Merge Overall Digest').item.json;\\nlet parsed;\\ntry {\\n  const content = response.choices[0].message.content;\\n  parsed = JSON.parse(content);\\n} catch (e) {\\n  parsed = {\\n    whatMoved: 'Summary unavailable — the LLM response could not be parsed.',\\n    whatShipped: '',\\n    whatIsBlocked: '',\\n    needsReview: '',\\n    sprintHealth: 'Unknown — check the digest workflow run for errors.'\\n  };\\n}\\nreturn [{ json: { summary: parsed, digest } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "7c10fac2-504d-4bab-8b0a-7cd8db1fba74", "name": "Build Slack Message Blocks", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [3872, 800], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const { summary, digest } = $json;\\nconst userMap = $('Set Config Fields').item.json.userMap || {};\\n\\nfunction mention(idOrLogin) {\\n  const slackId = userMap[idOrLogin];\\n  return slackId ? `<@${slackId}>` : (idOrLogin || 'unassigned');\\n}\\n\\nconst staleMentions = (digest.staleIssues || []).map(i => mention(i.assigneeAccountId || i.assignee));\\nconst reviewMentions = (digest.prsAwaitingReview || []).map(p => mention(p.author));\\nconst allMentions = [...new Set([...staleMentions, ...reviewMentions])].filter(m => m.startsWith('<@'));\\n\\nconst blocks = [\\n  { type: 'header', text: { type: 'plain_text', text: '📋 Engineering Daily Digest' } },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*Sprint health:* ${summary.sprintHealth}` } },\\n  { type: 'divider' },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*What moved*\\\\n${summary.whatMoved}` } },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*What shipped*\\\\n${summary.whatShipped}` } },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*What's blocked*\\\\n${summary.whatIsBlocked}` } },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*Needs review*\\\\n${summary.needsReview}` } },\\n  { type: 'divider' },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*Stale tickets (${(digest.staleIssues||[]).length})*\\\\n` + ((digest.staleIssues||[]).map(i => `• <${i.url}|${i.key}> — ${i.summary} (${i.daysStale}d, ${mention(i.assigneeAccountId || i.assignee)})`).join('\\\\n') || '_none_') } },\\n  { type: 'section', text: { type: 'mrkdwn', text: `*PRs awaiting review (${(digest.prsAwaitingReview||[]).length})*\\\\n` + ((digest.prsAwaitingReview||[]).map(p => `• <${p.url}|#${p.number} ${p.title}> — ${p.hoursOpen}h, ${mention(p.author)}`).join('\\\\n') || '_none_') } }\\n];\\n\\nif (allMentions.length) {\\n  blocks.push({ type: 'context', elements: [{ type: 'mrkdwn', text: `cc ${allMentions.join(' ')}` }] });\\n}\\n\\nreturn [{ json: { blocks, text: `Engineering Daily Digest — ${summary.sprintHealth}`, digest, summary } }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "1f88e1b8-6cb7-4173-9a1e-fb32e9ac8735", "name": "If Logging to Sheet Enabled", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "position": [4768, 784], "parameters": {"options": {}, "conditions": {"options": {"version": 1, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "sheet-cond-1", "operator": {"type": "boolean", "operation": "true", "singleValue": true}, "leftValue": "={{ $('Set Config Fields').item.json.sheetEnabled }}", "rightValue": true}]}}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "6273a267-6647-46a9-b5c1-2c7ea291e2ed", "name": "Append Row to Google Sheets", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets", "position": [4992, 688], "parameters": {"columns": {"value": {}, "schema": [{"id": "ok", "type": "string", "display": true, "removed": false, "required": false, "displayName": "ok", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": true}, {"id": "channel", "type": "string", "display": true, "removed": false, "required": false, "displayName": "channel", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": true}, {"id": "message", "type": "string", "display": true, "removed": false, "required": false, "displayName": "message", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": true}, {"id": "message_timestamp", "type": "string", "display": true, "removed": false, "required": false, "displayName": "message_timestamp", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": true}], "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData", "matchingColumns": [], "attemptToConvertTypes": false, "convertFieldsToString": false}, "options": {}, "operation": "append", "sheetName": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": 903721058, "cachedResultUrl": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yozEO983mOlmmCm0ujIVUsU46yop5D6HsN-VvL0dU2w/edit#gid=903721058", "cachedResultName": "Sheet4"}, "documentId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "1yozEO983mOlmmCm0ujIVUsU46yop5D6HsN-VvL0dU2w", "cachedResultUrl": "https://docs