/node/25564	Viidure Dashcam Android Application	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-272-07	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-29 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSuccessful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could allow attackers to access, modify, or delete sensitive user data and critical system files, potentially compromising the operation of the entire platform.\\nThe following versions of Viidure Dashcam Android Application are affected:\\nDashcam Android Application <=3.3.1.260403 (CVE-2026-94204, CVE-2026-96587)\\nCVSS\\nVendor\\nEquipment\\nVulnerabilities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nv3 10\\nViidure\\nViidure Dashcam Android Application\\nIncorrect Permission Assignm"}	verified	[]	Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could allow attackers to access, modify, or delete sensitive user data and critical system files, potentially compromising the operation of the entire platform.	["Attackers can exploit vulnerabilities to access and modify user data", "Potential compromise of the entire platform is a critical consequence"]	["Viidure Dashcam Android Application", "CVE-2026-94204", "CVE-2026-96587"]	["Android", "Dashcam application"]	["Security vulnerability", "Data breach"]	high	[]
/node/25560	VIVOTEK Camera Firmware	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-272-03	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-29 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSuccessful exploitation of this vulnerability may allow attackers to achieve remote command execution on affected devices, potentially with root privileges, leading to full compromise of the camera system.\\nThe following versions of VIVOTEK Camera Firmware are affected:\\nV Series model_FD9187 (CVE-2026-22755)\\nV Series model_FD9189 (CVE-2026-22755)\\nV Series model_FD9365 (CVE-2026-22755)\\nV Series model_FD9387 (CVE-2026-22755)\\nV Series model_FD9389 (CVE-2026-22755)\\nV Series model_FD"}	verified	[]	Exploitation of the identified vulnerabilities in VIVOTEK Camera Firmware may lead to remote command execution with root privileges, resulting in full compromise of the affected systems. The vulnerabilities specifically impact devices of the V Series models FD9187, FD9189, FD9365, FD9387, and FD9389.	["VIVOTEK Camera Firmware is affected by multiple CVEs", "Vulnerable devices include FD9187, FD9189, FD9365, FD9387, and FD9389", "Successful exploitation can lead to remote command execution with root privileges"]	["VIVOTEK", "FD9187", "FD9189", "FD9365", "FD9387", "FD9389"]	["Firmware", "Vulnerability", "Remote Command Execution"]	["Information Security", "Critical Vulnerabilities", "Remote Compromise"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/bitget-confirms-third-party-zero-day.html	Bitget Confirms Third-Party Zero-Day Behind $387.5 Million Cryptocurrency Theft	https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/bitget-confirms-third-party-zero-day.html	The Hacker News	2026-10-01 05:21:10+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Cryptocurrency exchange Bitget on Wednesday confirmed that attackers who stole $387.5 million last week exploited a zero-day flaw in third-party security products, citing ongoing investigation findings from SlowMist.\\n\\n\\"Their investigation identified malicious activity involving third-party security products, including a zero-day vulnerability, and recovered a customized tool used by the attacker"}	verified	[]	Bitget has confirmed that attackers who stole $387.5 million in cryptocurrency from the exchange last week used a zero-day flaw in third-party security products, primarily a customized tool developed by the attacker. Bitget's ongoing investigation has attributed the attack to malicious activity involving said third-party security products.	["Cryptocurrency exchange Bitget suffered a theft of $387.5 million", "Attacker exploited zero-day vulnerability in third-party security products", "Investigation suggests custom tool was used by attacker"]	["Bitget", "cryptocurrency theft", "third-party security products", "zero-day vulnerability", "customized tool"]	["cryptocurrency exchange", "third-party security products", "customized tool"]	["cybersecurity", "cryptocurrency", "hacking", "investigation"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/official-mcp-python-sdk-flaw-can-let.html	Official MCP Python SDK Flaw Can Let Malicious Servers Steal OAuth Credentials	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/official-mcp-python-sdk-flaw-can-let.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-29 06:08:25+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "A malicious MCP server could trick an application built on the official MCP Python SDK into handing over the OAuth credentials it uses to log in to a real service, the SDK's maintainers said in a security advisory.\\n\\nAffected versions sent the client secret, the authorization code, and the PKCE proof key to a token endpoint the attacker controlled. The fix is in versions 1.30.0 and"}	verified	[]	The official MCP Python SDK contains a security flaw allowing a malicious MCP server to steal OAuth credentials used by applications built with the SDK to log into real services.	["Malicious MCP server can trick applications built on the official MCP Python SDK into handing over OAuth credentials", "SDK's maintainers identified the vulnerability in a security advisory", "Affected versions have sent OAuth credentials to a controlled token endpoint by the attacker", "A fix is available in versions 1.30.0"]	["MCP Python SDK", "OAuth credentials", "MCP server", "real service", "official MCP Python SDK", "client secret", "authorization code", "PKCE proof key", "token endpoint"]	["Python SDK"]	["security", "OAuth", "token", "service", "server"]	medium	[]
/node/25229	Siemens Mendix Runtime (Update A)	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-209-02	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-24 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nThis advisory is revoked. Re-investigation confirmed the reported behavior is expected platform configuration and does not expose the protected attribute.\\nThe following versions of Siemens Mendix Runtime are affected:\\nSiemens Mendix Runtime vers:all/* (CVE-2026-7891)\\nCVSS\\nVendor\\nEquipment\\nVulnerabilities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nv3 9.1\\nSiemens\\nSiemens Mendix Runtime \\nInsecure Inherited Permissions\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nBackground\\nCritical Infrastructure Sectors: Critical Manufacturing\\nCountries/Areas Deployed: World"}	verified	[]	This advisory for Siemens Mendix Runtime (Update A) advises users to disregard the initial release as the issue does not pose a security threat, as the described vulnerability is expected configuration and does not expose protected attributes.	["The advisory is revoked and confirmed the reported issue is expected behavior and does not expose protected attributes.", "Siemens Mendix Runtime is affected by this vulnerability.", "The vulnerability, previously classified, has been downgraded from a critical severity to informational."]	["Siemens Mendix Runtime", "CVE-2026-7891", "Siemens", "Critical Infrastructure Sectors: Critical Manufacturing"]	["Siemens"]	["Siemens Mendix Runtime", "CVE-2026-7891", "Critical Manufacturing", "revoke advisory", "expected configuration", "does not expose", "protected attribute"]	low	[]
/node/25524	Siemens SIPLUS and SIMATIC Products	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-04	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nMultiple Siemens products are vulnerable to the \\"Copy Fail\\" vulnerability. Siemens has released new versions for several affected products and recommends to update to the latest versions. Siemens is preparing further fix versions and recommends specific countermeasures for products where fixes are not, or not yet available.\\nThe following versions of Siemens SIPLUS and SIMATIC Products are affected:\\nSIMATIC AX Runtime Core Linux Common Debian vers:all/* (CVE-2026-31431)\\nSIMATIC "}	verified	[]	Multiple Siemens products, specifically versions of SIMATIC AX and SIMATIC products, are affected by the 'Copy Fail' vulnerability. Siemens has released updated versions for several affected products and is preparing further fix versions for products where full fixes are not available yet. Recommendations include updating to the latest versions or implementing specific countermeasures.	["Multiple Siemens products are vulnerable to the 'Copy Fail' vulnerability", "Siemens released new versions for affected products", "Update to latest versions or implement specific countermeasures", "Further fix versions are being prepared by Siemens"]	["SIMATIC AX", "SIMATIC AX Runtime Core Linux Common Debian", "SIMATIC", "Siemens SIPLUS", "Copy Fail"]	["vulnerability", "vulnerability mitigation", "vulnerability management"]	["Information Security", "Vulnerability Announcements", "Vulnerability Updates"]	medium	[]
/node/25521	lwIP TCP/IP Stack MQTT Client Application	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-01	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-09-30 16:05:30.279+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSuccessful exploitation of this vulnerability could allow an attacker to gain full code execution on the device.\\nThe following versions of lwIP TCP/IP Stack MQTT Client Application are affected:\\nMQTT Client Application >=2.0.1|<=2.2.1 (CVE-2026-87121)\\nCVSS\\nVendor\\nEquipment\\nVulnerabilities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nv3 9.8\\nlwIP\\nlwIP TCP/IP Stack MQTT Client Application\\nOut-of-bounds Write\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nBackground\\nCritical Infrastructure Sectors: Chemical, Communications, Critical Manufacturing, Energy, Financia"}	verified	[]	Successful exploitation of CVE-2026-87121 could allow an attacker to gain full code execution on affected versions of the lwIP TCP/IP Stack MQTT Client Application. These versions are between 2.0.1 and 2.2.1 inclusive, affecting multiple critical infrastructure sectors such as Chemical, Communications, Critical Manufacturing, Energy, and Financial Services.	["Exploitation of affected lwIP TCP/IP Stack MQTT Client Application versions could lead to full code execution.", "Versions affected are MQTT Client Application >=2.0.1 <=2.2.1.", "Critical infrastructure sectors such as Energy, Chemical, Communications, Critical Manufacturing, and Financial Services are at risk."]	["CVE-2026-87121", "MQTT Client Application", "lwIP TCP/IP Stack", "Energy", "Chemical", "Communications", "Critical Manufacturing", "Financial Services"]	["lwIP"]	["Code Execution", "Critical Infrastructure", "Vulnerability", "Out-of-bounds Write"]	high	[]
/node/25523	Siemens Siveillance Control	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-03	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nA vulnerability has been identified in the Open Interface Services (OIS) web module affecting Siveillance Control and Siveillance Control Pro (versions OIS 3.x.y and OIS 4.x.y) . This vulnerability allows an attacker to upload arbitrary files, which can lead to unauthorized root-level access on the OIS server. Siemens has released patches and updates for Siveillance OIS to apply to the products that incorporate the OIS service, and recommends to update to the latest versions.\\nT"}	verified	[]	A vulnerability affecting Siemens Siveillance Control and Siveillance Control Pro web modules, specifically versions of OIS 3.x.y and OIS 4.x.y, has been identified. This vulnerability allows attackers to upload arbitrary files, resulting in unauthorized root access to the OIS server. Siemens has provided patches and advises users to update to the latest versions.	["Vulnerability in Open Interface Services (OIS) web module", "Affects Siveillance Control and Control Pro versions 3.x.y and 4.x.y", "Allows attackers to upload arbitrary files", "Can lead to unauthorized root-level access on OIS servers", "Siemens released patches and recommends updating to the latest versions"]	["Siemens Siveillance Control", "Siemens Siveillance Control Pro", "OIS (Open Interface Services)", "Open Interface Services (OIS) web module", "vulnerability", "authorized root-level access on the OIS server"]	["OIS (Open Interface Services)", "OIS web module"]	["vulnerability", "security patch", "root-level access"]	high	[]
