https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/know-your-enemy-browser-based-attack.html	Know Your Enemy: Browser-Based Attack Techniques in 2026	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/know-your-enemy-browser-based-attack.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 11:58:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Given that the browser is where business apps are accessed and used, it makes sense that attacks are happening there too. Most breaches today begin in a browser session. Often, they never leave it, with the entire attack chain from initial access to exfiltration playing out in the browser.\\n\\nHere are the six most dangerous techniques that should be on every security team's radar in 2026.\\n\\n1."}	verified	[]	This news item discusses the security threats faced by browsers as a primary entry point for business applications. It highlights that the number of browser-based attacks is increasing, with many breaches starting within a browser session and often remaining there. Six methods perceived as dangerous for security teams in 2026 are outlined.	["Browser-based attacks are common and often don't leave the browser.", "Increased use of business apps via browsers exposes them to security threats.", "Many breaches start in a browser session and can be conducted entirely within the browser."]	["browsers", "business apps", "security breaches", "attacks"]	["Browser Security", "Security Teams"]	["Security Threats", "Browser-Based Attacks", "2026 Predictions"]	medium	[]
