https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/101-malicious-npm-packages-add.html	101 Malicious npm Packages Add Developers' WhatsApp Accounts to Groups Without Consent	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/101-malicious-npm-packages-add.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-29 13:45:10+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Cybersecurity researchers have identified a cluster of 101 npm packages that are used to trap developers into a WhatsApp group subscriber campaign dubbed PhantomSub.\\n\\n\\"The malicious packages abuse the 'Baileys' WhatsApp open source project to add the victims to groups without their consent,\\" OX Security researchers Nir Zadok, Moshe Siman Tov Bustan, and Vitalii Chepurko said in a technical"}	verified	[]	Researchers from OX Security have discovered 101 npm packages that exploit the 'Baileys' WhatsApp open source project to automatically add developers to WhatsApp groups without their permission, potentially compromising their privacy.	["101 npm packages identified as malicious", "Automatically add victims to WhatsApp groups without consent", "Uses a WhatsApp open source project for the exploit", "Potential privacy violation for developers"]	["101 npm package", "Ox Security", "WhatsApp open source project", "Malicious package developer"]	["npm packages", "WhatsApp", "open source project", "security research"]	["malware", "security vulnerability", "privacy breach", "technology exploitation"]	medium	[]
