/node/25528	Siemens WTV676 and WTV776	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-08	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-09-30 16:05:30.279+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nThe products listed below contain a denial of service vulnerability that could allow an attacker to force the devices into protection mode under certain conditions. This disables remote connectivity functions (Web Access) to the devices. Siemens has released new versions for the affected products and recommends to update to the latest versions.\\nThe following versions of Siemens WTV676 and WTV776 are affected:\\nWTV676-HB6035 Web Interface vers:intdot/<3.94 (CVE-2026-89207)\\nWTV776"}	verified	[]	Siemens WTV676 and WTV776 products contain a denial of service vulnerability that can cause devices to enter protection mode, preventing remote connectivity functions. Siemens has released new versions to resolve this issue and recommend updating to the latest versions.	["Denial of service vulnerability found in Siemens WTV676 and WTV776 products", "Devices enter protection mode, blocking remote connectivity functions", "Siemens has released new versions to fix the issue", "Users are advised to update to the latest versions"]	["Siemens WTV676", "Siemens WTV776", "CVE-2026-89207", "Web Interface"]	["Software"]	["Vulnerability", "Denial of Service", "Remote Connectivity", "Software Update"]	high	[]
/node/25536	CISA Adds Four Known Exploited Vulnerabilities to Catalog	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/09/22/cisa-adds-four-known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-09-30 16:05:30.279+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "CISA has added four new vulnerabilities to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog, based on evidence of active exploitation.\\nCVE-2026-85102 Check Point Multiple Products Improper Certificate Validation Vulnerability\\nCVE-2026-93616 Check Point Multiple Products Path Traversal Vulnerability\\nCVE-2026-93952 Arista VeloCloud Orchestrator Improper Input Validation Vulnerability\\nCVE-2026-94127 F5 BIG-IP APM Heap-based Buffer Overflow Vulnerability\\nThese types of vulnerabilities are a frequen"}	verified	[]	The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has updated its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog by adding four known exploited vulnerabilities affecting multiple products by Check Point, Arista, and F5. These vulnerabilities include issues related to certificate validation, input validation, and heap-based buffer overflow that have been exploited in the wild.	["Four known exploited vulnerabilities added to the U.S. CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog", "Check Point, Arista, F5 products affected", "Vulnerabilities include improper certificate validation, input validation, and heap-based buffer overflow"]	["U.S. CISA", "CVE-2026-85102", "CVE-2026-93616", "CVE-2026-93952", "CVE-2026-94127", "Check Point", "Arista", "F5", "Certificate Validation", "Path Traversal", "Improper Input Validation", "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"]	["Check Point", "Arista", "F5", "Network Security", "Input Validation", "Buffer Overflow"]	["CISA", "Exploited Vulnerabilities", "KEV Catalog", "Security Updates", "IT Security"]	medium	[]
/node/25527	Siemens SIMOVE Fleetmanager and SIPLANT	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-07	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-09-30 16:05:30.279+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSIMOVE Fleetmanager and SIPLANT contain a path traversal vulnerability that could allow an attacker to access files outside of intended scope. Siemens has released new versions for the affected products and recommends to update to the latest versions.\\nThe following versions of Siemens SIMOVE Fleetmanager and SIPLANT are affected:\\nSIMOVE Fleetmanager V3.1 vers:intdot/<3.1.13 (CVE-2026-67367)\\nSIMOVE Fleetmanager V3.2 vers:intdot/<3.2.4 (CVE-2026-67367)\\nSIMOVE Fleetmanager V3.3 ve"}	verified	[]	Siemens SIMOVE Fleetmanager and SIPLANT software have been found to contain path traversal vulnerabilities, which could enable attackers to access files outside their intended scope. Siemens has issued new versions and advises users to update to the latest versions to mitigate this risk.	["Path traversal vulnerability found in Siemens SIMOVE Fleetmanager and SIPLANT", "Affected versions include SIMOVE Fleetmanager V3.1 <3.1.13, V3.2 <3.2.4, and V3.3", "Siemens has released updated versions to address the vulnerabilities"]	["Siemens SIMOVE Fleetmanager", "Siemens SIPLANT", "CVE-2026-67367", "V3.1", "V3.2", "V3.3"]	["Software vulnerability", "Path traversal vulnerability"]	["Software Security", "Vulnerability", "Software Updates"]	high	[]
/node/25529	OpenPLC Runtime v3	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-265-09	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-22 12:00:00+00	2026-09-30 16:05:30.279+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSuccessful exploitation of this vulnerability could allow an attacker to hijack session cookies and issue state-changing requests as an operator which would allow the attacker to control the programmable logic controller and the physical processes it drives.\\nThe following versions of OpenPLC Runtime v3 are affected:\\nOpenPLC 3 (CVE-2026-88020)\\nCVSS\\nVendor\\nEquipment\\nVulnerabilities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nv3 6.1\\nAutonomy Logic\\nOpenPLC Runtime v3\\nImproper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Gener"}	verified	[]	The news snippet discusses a vulnerability in the OpenPLC Runtime v3 version, where successful exploitation could allow attackers to hijack session cookies, control operator privileges, and manipulate physical processes controlled by programmable logic controllers. The vulnerability is considered severe, as it involves improper neutralization of input during web page generation and affects multiple versions of the software. The CVSS score, vendor, equipment, and relevant vulnerabilities are also mentioned.	["This vulnerability could allow attackers to hijack session cookies and control physical processes.", "The vulnerability involves improper input neutralization during web page generation.", "Multiple versions of OpenPLC Runtime v3 are affected.", "The severity is considered high as it could lead to physical process manipulation."]	["OpenPLC Runtime v3", "CVE-2026-88020", "Autonomy Logic", "OpenPLC"]	["OpenPLC Runtime v3", "Web Page"]	["vulnerability", "OpenPLC", "CVSS", "hardware control", "information security"]	high	[]
