https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-exploit-netscaler-flaw-for.html	Attackers Exploit NetScaler Flaw for Root Access, Deploy WHIPSHOT and SLAPSHOT	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-exploit-netscaler-flaw-for.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 08:24:35+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Unknown threat actors have been observed exploiting a newly patched security flaw in Citrix NetScaler ADC and NetScaler Gateway appliances to target organizations in North America and Europe.\\n\\nThe activity, observed by Mandiant Consulting and Google Threat Intelligence Group (GTIG) in September 2026, has targeted government, financial services, technology, education, and legal and professional"}	verified	[]	Unknown threat actors exploited a NetScaler appliance security flaw to gain root access and deploy malware targeting organizations in North America and Europe. This activity was observed by Mandiant Consulting and Google Threat Intelligence Group (GTIG) in September 2026.	["NetScaler appliance security flaw exploited", "Targeted organizations in North America and Europe", "Included government, financial services, technology, education, and legal sectors", "Gained root access and deployed malware"]	["NetScaler", "Citrix NetScaler ADC and NetScaler Gateway appliances", "Mandiant Consulting", "Google Threat Intelligence Group (GTIG)", "Unknown threat actors", "September 2026"]	["Citrix NetScaler", "Google Threat Intelligence Group"]	["Security flaw", "Malware", "Threat actors", "Government", "Financial services", "Technology", "Education", "Legal and professional"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/citrix-netscaler-cve-2026-88772-exploit.html	Citrix NetScaler CVE-2026-88772 Exploit Details Show Pre-Auth Path to Shellcode Execution	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/citrix-netscaler-cve-2026-88772-exploit.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 05:30:30+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Cybersecurity researchers have disclosed technical details of a recently patched critical security flaw in Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway that has come under active exploitation in the wild.\\n\\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-88772 (CVSS score: 9.5), has been described as a memory overflow bug in the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol handling that's rooted in the NetScaler"}	verified	[]	Researchers have revealed details about a highly critical security vulnerability in Citrix NetScaler products. CVE-2026-88772, with a CVSS score of 9.5, affects the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) handling and can be exploited to execute shellcode without authentication, causing serious damage to affected systems.	["CVE-2026-88772 is a critical security flaw in Citrix NetScaler products.", "The vulnerability affects the Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) protocol handling.", "The exploit does not require authentication.", "CVE-2026-88772 has a CVSS score of 9.5, indicating the highest severity.", "The vulnerability is actively being exploited in the wild."]	["CVE-2026-88772", "Citrix NetScaler", "Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS)"]	["CVE", "CVSS", "NetScaler", "DTLS"]	["Security Vulnerability", "Critical", "Exploit", "Patch", "Active Exploitation"]	critical	[]
