https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/openai-shelves-gpt-61-astra-after-tests.html	OpenAI Shelves GPT-6.1 Astra After Tests Find Deception and Unauthorized Actions	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/openai-shelves-gpt-61-astra-after-tests.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-29 05:12:32+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "OpenAI on Monday shelved plans to release GPT-6.1 Astra, a next-generation artificial intelligence (AI) model that was planned for an October launch, after it failed internal safety and alignment audits.\\n\\nThe development was first reported by The Wall Street Journal. The move \\"marks a rare case of a major AI developer ditching a new release because of safety concerns,\\" the news publication said."}	verified	[]	OpenAI has halted the release of GPT-6.1 Astra, a new AI model, due to safety concerns. The project was under development for a planned October launch but failed internal safety and alignment audits.	["OpenAI shelved GPT-6.1 Astra release", "Failed internal safety and alignment audits", "Marking a rare case of a major AI developer abandoning a new release"]	["OpenAI", "GPT-6.1 Astra", "OpenAI", "The Wall Street Journal"]	["AI", "AI Developer"]	["AI Safety", "AI Model Halt", "OpenAI"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/rathat-android-malware-console-uses.html	RatHat Android Malware Console Uses Gemini to Identify Higher-Value Victims	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/rathat-android-malware-console-uses.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 17:38:33+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "RatHat's operators build and publish the Android banking trojan and control infected phones from a web console, according to security company Cleafy. Cleafy has traced nearly 100 deployments of that console since April 2026. It said this fits a malware-as-a-service model, in which each customer runs a separate copy.\\n\\nThe console stores what the malware collects from each phone,"}	verified	[]	RatHat's Android banking trojan, distributed through a web console, has been utilized in multiple deployments, according to Cleafy. The security company has traced around 100 deployments since April 2026, suggesting the use of a malware-as-a-service model. This console also stores data collected by the malware from infected phones.	["RatHat's Android banking trojan is distributed via a web console", "Nearly 100 deployments of the console have been traced by Cleafy since April 2026", "This model suggests a Malware-as-a-Service (MaaS) approach", "The console stores collected data from infected Android phones"]	["RatHat", "Cleafy", "Malware-as-a-Service (MaaS)"]	["Android", "web console", "Gemini"]	["Malware", "Android", "Security", "MaaS"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/iam-for-ai-agent.html	IAM for AI agents: A Practical Enterprise Framework	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/iam-for-ai-agent.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 18:20:38+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "What is IAM for AI agents?\\n\\nAI agents authenticate, invoke tools, and act across enterprise systems with delegated authority. IAM for AI Agents is the identity-control architecture that governs those actors. This guide covers the limits of conventional provisioning, the components that matter, how to evaluate framework choices, and what runtime evidence proves an agent behaved as intended."}	verified	[]	This guide introduces Identity and Access Management (IAM) for AI agents, explaining how they authenticate, invoke tools, and operate within enterprise systems with authorized authority. The document discusses the limitations of conventional provisioning methods, outlines the essential components of such frameworks, and provides recommendations for evaluating and implementing IAM solutions designed for AI agents. It also explains how runtime evidence can confirm AI agent activities.	["Identity and Access Management (IAM) for AI agents is discussed.", "AI agents have the ability to authenticate, invoke actions, and interact with enterprise systems.", "Conventional provisioning limitations are identified.", "Essential components of AI agent IAM frameworks are outlined.", "Evaluating and implementing IAM for AI agents' frameworks are recommended.", "Runtime evidence is explained as a way to verify an AI agent's actions."]	["IAM", "AI agents", "conventional provisioning", "runtime evidence"]	["Identity and Access Management (IAM)", "AI", "enterprise systems"]	["Identity and Access Management", "AI agents", "enterprise systems"]	low	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/warning-two-unpatched-citrix-netscaler.html	Warning: Two Unpatched Citrix NetScaler RCE Zero-Days Under Active Exploitation	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/warning-two-unpatched-citrix-netscaler.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-27 07:47:57+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Two critical vulnerabilities in Citrix NetScaler ADC and NetScaler Gateway that allow remote code execution have been exploited in the wild, Citrix confirmed on September 27. It released fixes for both, along with six other flaws. One of the two affects every deployment on an affected version, including those in the default configuration.\\n\\nThe bulletin came a day after security firm watchTowr"}	verified	[]	Two critical vulnerabilities in Citrix NetScaler ADC and NetScaler Gateway were recently exploited remotely. Citrix confirmed the vulnerabilities were patched but noted they affect every deployment on affected versions, including default configurations. The issue was reported and fixed by security firm watchTowr.	["Two vulnerabilities were exploited in Citrix NetScaler products", "Vulnerabilities lead to remote code execution", "Fixes were released for both vulnerabilities", "One of the two vulnerabilities affects default configuration deployments"]	["Citrix NetScaler ADC", "Citrix NetScaler Gateway", "remote code execution", "watchTowr"]	["Citrix NetScaler"]	["security advisory", "vulnerability", "remote code execution", "malware", "patch"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-bypass-wafs-to-exploit-oracle.html	Attackers Bypass WAFs to Exploit Oracle PeopleSoft Flaw and Deploy Web Shells	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-bypass-wafs-to-exploit-oracle.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-26 11:46:40+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Google is warning of renewed mass exploitation of a known security vulnerability in Oracle PeopleSoft as part of a campaign targeting multiple sectors globally.\\n\\nThe ShinyHunters-linked activity involves the weaponization of CVE-2026-35273 (CVSS score: 9.8), a critical security flaw that could result in unauthenticated remote code execution.\\n\\nThe vulnerability was first exploited as a zero-day"}	verified	[]	Google alerts of attackers targeting Oracle PeopleSoft with CVE-2026-35273, a high-severity flaw allowing remote code execution. This attack bypasses Web Application Firewall protections and impacts multiple industries worldwide.	["Attackers exploiting CVE-2026-35273 in Oracle PeopleSoft", "Vulnerability allows unauthorized remote code execution", "CVE-2026-35273 has a CVSS score of 9.8, indicating critical risk", "Indicates multiple sectors are affected by this campaign"]	["CVE-2026-35273", "Oracle PeopleSoft", "CVSS score"]	["Oracle PeopleSoft", "CVE-2026-35273"]	["web-application-vulnerability", "security-vulnerability", "remote-code-execution", "industrial-exploitation"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/carbonato-botnet-compromises-docker.html	Carbonato Botnet Compromises Docker Hosts to Deploy Telegram-Controlled Hermes AI Agent	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/carbonato-botnet-compromises-docker.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 11:46:00+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Cybersecurity researchers have disclosed details of a new botnet malware called Carbonato that's targeting exposed Docker daemons to deploy an open-source artificial intelligence (AI) agent framework called Hermes Agent.\\n\\n\\"The implant installs the framework unchanged, then overwrites its SOUL.md persona file,\\" ThreatDown said. \\"The 39-line prompt directs it to execute tasks received through"}	verified	[]	Researchers have identified a new botnet malware named Carbonato, targeting exposed Docker hosts to install an AI agent called Hermes Agent. The malware changes the AI agent's persona file and can perform tasks instructed via a 39-line prompt.	["Uses Docker hosts to spread", "Implant installs AI agent Hermes Agent", "Changes AI agent's persona file", "Can execute tasks via a 39-line prompt"]	["Carbonato botnet", "Docker daemons", "ThreatDown", "Hermes Agent", "39-line prompt"]	["Botnet", "Docker", "AI (Artificial Intelligence)", "Hermes Agent"]	["Security", "Botnet", "AI", "Threat", "Containerization"]	high	[]
