https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-abuse-chatgpt-custom-gpts-to.html	Attackers Abuse ChatGPT Custom GPTs to Deliver RAT via ClickFix Lures	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/attackers-abuse-chatgpt-custom-gpts-to.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 15:00:15+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Threat actors are abusing ChatGPT Custom GPTs to disguise them as legitimate product offerings and direct unsuspecting victims to malicious sites that employ ClickFix lures to deliver malware.\\n\\nHuntress, which observed the activity in late September 2026, said it marks the abuse of yet another feature in trusted artificial intelligence (AI) platforms. Prior campaigns have weaponized shared"}	verified	[]	Threat actors are abusing ChatGPT Custom GPTs to disguise malicious links as legitimate offers. This has led to victims being directed to sites using ClickFix lures, which deliver malware.	["Threat actors are abusing ChatGPT Custom GPTs for malicious purposes", "Legitimate-looking links are used to direct users to malicious sites", "ClickFix lures are employed to deliver malware"]	["ChatGPT", "Threat actors", "ClickFix lures", "malware"]	["ChatGPT", "AI platforms"]	["malware", "AI abuse", "Threat actor tactics"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/ai-coding-agents-exposed-13000-internal.html	AI Coding Agents Exposed 13,000 Internal Images, Including Billing Records, on GitHub	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/ai-coding-agents-exposed-13000-internal.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 11:30:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "AI coding agents asked to share screenshots of code changes for review have put internal company images in public GitHub repositories, security company Glow said.\\n\\nIts researchers found more than 13,000 internal images from developers at over 300 organizations, including customer billing records and screens of features not yet released. In most cases, they sat under developers' personal accounts"}	verified	[]	Researchers from security company Glow discovered that AI coding agents sharing code changes screenshots on GitHub inadvertently exposed more than 13,000 internal images from developers at over 300 organizations. These images included customer billing records and screens of features not yet released, stored under personal accounts.	["AI coding agents exposed internal images on GitHub.", "Included images include billing records and internal features.", "Over 300 organizations were affected.", "Images were stored under developers' personal accounts."]	["AI coding agents", "GitHub", "security company Glow", "developers", "organizations"]	["AI", "GitHub", "security"]	["security", "AI exposure", "company image leaks", "GitHub misuse"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/french-tax-data-theft-using-stolen.html	French Tax Data Theft Using Stolen Staff Passwords Went Undetected for Seven Weeks	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/french-tax-data-theft-using-stolen.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-29 17:47:01+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "An attacker used stolen passwords of staff at France's tax administration to take tax data on hundreds of thousands of taxpayers and businesses in June and July.\\n\\nNeither the tax administration nor France's national cybersecurity agency saw the data leave. The attack was not sophisticated, the agency, ANSSI, says in a report (in French) published on Tuesday: it worked because of weak"}	verified	[]	A data breach occurred when an attacker exploited stolen staff passwords to access and steal tax data for hundreds of thousands of taxpayers and businesses in France's tax administration. Neither the administration nor the national cybersecurity agency detected the unauthorized data exfiltration for seven weeks, despite the reported lack of sophistication in the attack.	["Stolen staff passwords used for data theft", "Attackers accessed data for thousands of taxpayers and businesses", "Data exfiltration not detected for over a month", "Weak authentication system likely the cause of breach"]	["France", "tax administration", "national cybersecurity agency (ANSSI)", "tax data", "staff passwords"]	["Stolen passwords", "Authentication system"]	["Data Breach", "Weak Authentication", "National Tax Administration", "Cybersecurity"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/apple-patches-coregraphics-flaw.html	Apple Patches CoreGraphics Flaw Possibly Exploited in Targeted Attacks	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/apple-patches-coregraphics-flaw.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 19:18:01+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Apple has released security updates to address a vulnerability in older versions of iOS, iPadOS, and macOS that it said may have been exploited in targeted attacks.\\n\\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-86950, refers to an out-of-bounds write impacting the CoreGraphics component that could lead to arbitrary code execution when processing a maliciously crafted file.\\n\\nThe iPhone maker said the"}	verified	[]	Apple has released security updates to address a vulnerability in iOS, iPadOS, and macOS. The CVE-2026-86950 vulnerability affects CoreGraphics and may have been exploited in targeted attacks for arbitrary code execution from a maliciously crafted file.	["Apple released security updates", "Vulnerability in CoreGraphics", "Potential targeted attacks", "CVE-2026-86950 tracking number", "May lead to arbitrary code execution"]	["Apple", "CoreGraphics", "CVE-2026-86950"]	["iOS", "iPadOS", "macOS"]	["security", "vulnerability", "arbitrary code execution", "vandalism"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/webinar-how-to-govern-ai-agents-reduce.html	Webinar: How to Govern AI Agents, Reduce Excessive Access, and Control Shadow AI	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/webinar-how-to-govern-ai-agents-reduce.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 11:58:00+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "AI agents are moving into production faster than security teams can govern them. They are connecting to apps, handling data, calling APIs, and acting across business systems—often without the same controls applied to human users.\\n\\nAccording to Okta’s Global CISO Insights 2026 report, only 47% of CISOs are confident they can identify every AI agent in their environment. Even among those who feel"}	verified	[]	The news discusses the rapid adoption of AI agents into production environments and the lag in governance and security measures, resulting in concerns about uncontrolled access and potential risks.	["AI agents are moving into production faster than security teams can control them", "AI agents often operate across various business systems without adequate security controls", "Only 47% of CISOs feel confident identifying all AI agents in their environments"]	["Okta's Global CISO Insights 2026"]	["AI agents", "CISOs", "Security teams"]	["AI governance", "Security", "AI adoption", "CISO confidence"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/zero-trust-for-ai-agents-starts-with.html	Zero Trust for AI Agents Starts With Fixing Zero Visibility	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/zero-trust-for-ai-agents-starts-with.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-26 10:30:00+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "The way we talk about AI agents is shifting, and the way we implement them requires an even more fundamental shift. While earlier discourse focused on how quickly organizations could stand up agents and how much productivity they could promise, a string of recent incidents, including a widely discussed intrusion at Hugging Face during an evaluation of OpenAI agents, has spurred organizations to"}	verified	[]	The focus on AI agents is shifting from quick deployment and productivity promises to addressing visibility and security concerns after recent incidents highlighted the potential for misconfigured AI systems.	["Organizations are adopting a more security-focused approach to AI agents due to past incidents.", "Past discussions prioritized rapid deployment and productivity gains over security measures.", "Notable recent incidents highlighted the potential risks of AI systems, emphasizing the importance of security and visibility."]	["Hugging Face", "OpenAI agents", "Organizations", "Incidents"]	["AI agents", "security measures", "visibility"]	["AI Agents", "Security", "Incidents", "Zero Trust"]	medium	[]
/node/25552	Critical Zero-Day Vulnerabilities Exploited in Citrix NetScaler ADC, Gateway	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/09/27/critical-zero-day-vulnerabilities-exploited-citrix-netscaler-adc-gateway	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-09-27 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "CISA is amplifying Citrix’s disclosure of eight new vulnerabilities affecting Citrix NetScaler ADC and Citrix NetScaler Gateway products: CVE-2026-88771, CVE-2026-88772, CVE-2026-88773, CVE-2026-88774, CVE-2026-88775, CVE-2026-88776, CVE-2026-88777, and CVE-2026-88778. \\nCISA has added CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772 to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog. Both are critical, zero-day vulnerabilities that can independently enable remote code execution. CISA has received reports and"}	verified	[]	Critical vulnerabilities in Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway products have been disclosed. Eight new vulnerabilities, including CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772, have been classified as critical zero-day vulnerabilities. CISA has marked CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772 as Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV), indicating they have been exploited.	["Critical zero-day vulnerabilities in Citrix NetScaler products", "CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772 added to Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV)", "CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772 classified as critical"]	["Citrix NetScaler ADC", "Citrix NetScaler Gateway", "CVE-2026-88771", "CVE-2026-88772", "CVE-2026-88777"]	["NetScaler ADC", "NetScaler Gateway"]	["vulnerability disclosure", "zero-day vulnerabilities", "critical vulnerabilities", "CISA", "remote code execution"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/openai-disrupts-reasoning-extraction.html	OpenAI Disrupts Reasoning Extraction Campaign Linked to Moonshot AI Associates	https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/openai-disrupts-reasoning-extraction.html	The Hacker News	2026-10-01 10:42:36+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "OpenAI on Wednesday said it identified and disrupted a coordinated distillation campaign that was designed to illicitly extract protected reasoning from its artificial intelligence (AI) models.\\n\\nA \\"core cluster of the activity,\\" going back to the first week of July, has been attributed to individuals associated with Moonshot AI, a Chinese AI company based in Beijing. It did not cite any"}	verified	[]	OpenAI detected and halted a data-stealing scheme aimed at obtaining protected reasoning from its AI models. The campaign, dating back to mid-July, was linked to a team associated with the Chinese AI company Moonshot AI. OpenAI did not provide further details or name specific participants.	["OpenAI disrupted a reasoning extraction scheme", "Campaign involved illicitly obtaining protected reasoning from AI models", "Activity started in the first week of July", "Linked to individuals associated with Moonshot AI, a Chinese company"]	["OpenAI", "Moonshot AI", "Chinese AI company", "Artificial Intelligence (AI)", "artificial intelligence models", "Reasoning extraction"]	["Artificial Intelligence", "Chinese companies"]	["AI", "disruption", "data-stealing", "intelligence", "cymatics"]	medium	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/cisa-says-attackers-are-exploiting-two.html	CISA Says Attackers Are Exploiting Two Critical Citrix NetScaler Flaws Globally	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/cisa-says-attackers-are-exploiting-two.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-28 07:21:49+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) on Sunday added two critical Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway flaws to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, following reports of active exploitation.\\n\\nThe vulnerabilities are listed below -\\n\\n\\n  CVE-2026-88771 (CVSS score: 9.5) - An improper input validation vulnerability that could allow an unauthenticated attacker to"}	verified	[]	The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has added two critical Citrix NetScaler vulnerabilities, CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772, to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog. These vulnerabilities are associated with improper input validation, which can be exploited by unauthenticated attackers, to achieve a CVSS score of 9.5. The vulnerabilities have been reported to be being exploited actively.	["CISA added two critical Citrix NetScaler vulnerabilities to its KEV catalog", "CVE-2026-88771 has a CVSS score of 9.5", "Vulnerabilities can be exploited by unauthenticated attackers", "Active exploitation of these vulnerabilities has been reported"]	["CISA", "Citrix NetScaler", "CVE-2026-88771", "CVE-2026-88772", "Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA)", "CVSS score"]	["Citrix NetScaler", "CVE"]	["vulnerabilities", "active exploitation", "security vulnerabilities", "cybersecurity", "cybersecurity and infrastructure security agency (cisa)"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/us-focused-csuite-phishing-steals.html	US-Focused CSuite Phishing Steals Microsoft 365 Sessions and Deploys RMM Tools for Remote Access	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/us-focused-csuite-phishing-steals.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-30 10:45:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "ANY.RUN researchers traced a US-focused CSuite phishing campaign across 351 sandbox analyses, with 51% of submissions coming from the United States. Technology, manufacturing, government, and consulting organizations showed the highest exposure.\\n\\nBy combining Microsoft 365 session theft with remote-access tool deployment, CSuite can turn a phishing incident into broader account compromise, fraud"}	verified	[]	A US-focused phishing campaign targeting Corporate Suite employees has been identified. This cyber threat has resulted in the theft of Microsoft 365 sessions and enabled remote access tool deployment, with the campaign being traced in 351 sandbox analyses. The highest exposed organizations include technology, manufacturing, government, and consulting firms.	["Phishing campaign targeting US-based Corporate Suite employees", "Theft of Microsoft 365 sessions facilitated by remote-access tool deployment", "Campaign identified in 351 sandbox analyses", "Target organizations include technology, manufacturing, government, and consulting firms"]	["Microsoft 365", "Remote-access tools", "Phishing campaign", "US-based Corporate Suite employees", "Technology", "Manufacturing", "Government", "Consulting"]	["Microsoft 365", "Phishing", "Remote-access tools"]	["Cybersecurity", "Phishing", "Remote access", "US-based organizations"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/new-spectre-v2-btr-attack-leaks-linux.html	New Spectre-v2 BTR Attack Leaks Linux Memory Despite Existing Defenses	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/new-spectre-v2-btr-attack-leaks-linux.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-29 17:20:17+00	2026-10-02 16:05:30.97+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "A group of academics from VUSec and Scuola Superiore Sant'Anna have disclosed details of a new Spectre CPU vulnerability variant that affects Just-In-Time (JIT) engines present in web browsers, language runtimes, and the operating system kernel, across multiple CPU vendors.\\n\\nThe new Spectre v2 variant has been codenamed Branch Target Reuse (BTR).\\n\\n\\"The key insight is that, while modern CPUs"}	verified	[]	Academics have revealed a new Spectre-v2 CPU vulnerability called Branch Target Reuse (BTR) that impacts JIT engines in web browsers, language runtimes, and the operating system kernel across multiple CPU vendors. This highlights a significant vulnerability in computer security.	["New Spectre-v2 variant affects JIT engines in web browsers, language runtimes, and OS kernels", "The vulnerability is known as Branch Target Reuse (BTR)", "Affects multiple CPU vendors and is considered serious"]	["Spectre-v2", "Branch Target Reuse (BTR)", "JIT engines", "web browsers", "language runtimes", "Operating system kernel", "multiple CPU vendors"]	["CPU", "vulnerability"]	["Security", "Computer Science", "Computer Hardware", "Operating Systems", "Security Vulnerability"]	high	[]
https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/elementor-csrf-flaw-lets-attackers-take.html	Elementor CSRF Flaw Lets Attackers Take Over Sites After Admin Clicks Crafted Link	https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/elementor-csrf-flaw-lets-attackers-take.html	The Hacker News	2026-09-26 09:55:22+00	2026-10-02 15:30:29.694+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "info@thehackernews.com (The Hacker News)", "snippet": "Details have emerged about a high-severity security flaw in the Elementor Website Builder WordPress plugin that could be exploited by an unauthenticated attacker to create rogue administrator accounts and take control of a site.\\n\\nThe cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability, which has yet to be assigned a CVE identifier, carries a CVSS score of 8.8 out of 10.0. It only affects versions"}	verified	[]	A high-severity CSRF vulnerability in the Elementor Website Builder plugin for WordPress has been discovered. This vulnerability, not yet given a CVE identifier, can be exploited by attackers without authentication to create rogue admin accounts and seize control of affected sites. The vulnerability's CVSS score is 8.8, indicating a very high risk. It's only affected by certain versions of the plugin.	["Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) vulnerability in Elementor plugin", "Allows attackers to create rogue admin accounts without authentication", "Vulnerability impacts certain versions of the Elementor plugin", "CVSS score of 8.8, indicating high severity", "No CVE identifier yet assigned to the vulnerability"]	["Elementor", "WordPress", "CSRF", "cross-site request forgery", "admin accounts", "control of site", "unauthenticated attacker", "rogue administrator accounts"]	["Elementor", "WordPress", "CSRF"]	["security", "vulnerability", "Elementor", "WordPress", "CSRF attack"]	high	[]
/node/25572	Johnson Controls EasyIO Neo Series EC and CW Controllers	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-274-04	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-10-01 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "View CSAF\\nSummary\\nSuccessful exploitation of this vulnerability could allow an attacker to gain access to sensitive information that could be used to conduct further attacks against the system.\\nThe following versions of Johnson Controls EasyIO Neo Series EC and CW Controllers are affected:\\nEasyIO Neo Series EC Controllers V3.3b63 (CVE-2026-64892)\\nEasyIO Neo Series EC Controllers V3.3b62 (CVE-2026-64892)\\nEasyIO Neo Series CW Controllers V3.3b25 (CVE-2026-64892)\\nEasyIO Neo Series CW Controllers V3"}	verified	[]	Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could grant an attacker unauthorized access to sensitive information, potentially leading to further attacks on the system. The vulnerabilities affect specific versions of Johnson Controls EasyIO Neo Series controllers.	["Sensitive information may be accessed by attackers", "Attacker could launch further attacks based on obtained information", "Affected versions include V3.3b63, V3.3b62, V3.3b25 of EC and CW Controllers"]	["Johnson Controls EasyIO Neo Series", "V3.3b63", "V3.3b62", "V3.3b25", "EC Controllers", "CW Controllers"]	["Vulnerability", "Exploitation", "Access", "Sensitive Information", "Attacker", "Further Attacks", "System"]	["Vulnerability", "Exploit", "Access Control", "Sensitive Data", "Security Patch", "Cybersecurity"]	high	[]
/node/25579	CISA Adds One Known Exploited Vulnerability to Catalog	https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/10/01/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog	CISA Cybersecurity Alerts	2026-10-01 12:00:00+00	2026-10-02 16:05:31.031+00	cybersecurity	{"author": "CISA", "snippet": "CISA has added one new vulnerability to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog, based on evidence of active exploitation.\\nCVE-2026-104286 Fortinet FortiMail Path Traversal Vulnerability\\nThis type of vulnerability is a frequent attack vector for malicious cyber actors and poses significant risks to the federal enterprise. \\nBinding Operational Directive (BOD) 26-04: Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk establishes vulnerability management requirements for Federal Civilian Executi"}	verified	[]	CISA announced the addition of one known exploited vulnerability (CVE-2026-104286) from Fortinet's FortiMail software to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog. This vulnerability, which entails a Path Traversal issue, is considered a significant risk and frequent attack vector for malicious actors.	["Known Exploited Vulnerability added to CISA's catalog", "CVE-2026-104286", "Path Traversal issue in Fortinet FortiMail software"]	["CISA", "Fortinet", "FortiMail", "CVE-2026-104286"]	["CVE", "Fortinet", "FortiMail"]	["cybersecurity", "vulnerability", "CISA", "Fortinet"]	high	[]
