 "473db1b5-eb28-4d4d-9109-94946b79c60d", "name": "wait 5 sec1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait", "position": [4848, 3320], "webhookId": "238c4bf2-68f1-4b34-9ba3-fae3f80f3d61", "parameters": {}, "typeVersion": 1.1}, {"id": "c2705d3e-4611-4e18-a13c-3799ec7bf59f", "name": "Merge1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [6512, 320], "parameters": {"mode": "combine", "options": {}, "combineBy": "combineByPosition"}, "typeVersion": 3.2}, {"id": "5d8628ec-011a-4822-8cb6-a5cb7b2095ea", "name": "Split Out3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitOut", "position": [944, 320], "parameters": {"options": {}, "fieldToSplitOut": "list"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "f759963f-467d-45e0-90ed-1d02548f75d1", "name": "Code in JavaScript", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "onError": "continueErrorOutput", "position": [6512, 2320], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const item = $input.item.json;\\nconst url = item.list[0].company_linkedin_url || '';\\nconst username = url.split(/\\\\/(?:company|compnay|in)\\\\//)[1]?.replace(/\\\\/$/, '') ?? '';\\n\\nreturn {\\n  ...item.list[0],\\n  company_username: username\\n};"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "3e4ba940-0600-4aab-aabb-8ad53f883551", "name": "Call Anthropic API", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "onError": "continueErrorOutput", "disabled": true, "position": [2120, 4320], "parameters": {"url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={\\"model\\":\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\",\\"max_tokens\\":1500,\\"cache_control\\":{\\"type\\":\\"ephemeral\\"},\\"system\\":\\"<instructions>\\\\nYou are an expert cold email writer. You write short, human emails that feel like a quick note from a real person, not a pitch from a company.\\\\n\\\\nYou have access to a prospect briefing prepared by a research analyst. This briefing is your primary source. It contains the prospect's pain points, what they care about, a personalisation angle, and a conversation hook, all pre-filtered through the client's services.\\\\n\\\\nUse the briefing first. Only fall back to raw posts or industry defaults if the briefing is thin or says \\\\\\"weak fit.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n<raw_posts_fallback>\\\\nOnly use these if the briefing fields are empty, say \\\\\\"weak fit\\\\\\", or say \\\\\\"posts are too generic to personalise from.\\\\\\" Otherwise ignore this section entirely.\\\\n\\\\n<writing_priority>\\\\nThis is the order you follow when building the email:\\\\n\\\\n1. Use the briefing's personalisation_angle for the opening paragraph. This is a specific thing from their posts that was pre-selected for you. Reference it naturally like a peer who read it and had a real reaction.\\\\n\\\\n2. Use the briefing's pain_points for the second paragraph. These have already been filtered to match the client's services. Name the pain in plain language. Do not name the product.\\\\n\\\\n3. Use the briefing's conversation_hook to guide your tone and framing throughout.\\\\n\\\\n4. If the briefing says \\\\\\"weak fit\\\\\\" in service_connection, do NOT write the email. Set cold_email to \\\\\\"weak fit - no relevant service connection found.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n5. If has_posts is false AND the briefing fields are mostly empty, set cold_email to \\\\\\"no data found.\\\\\\"\\\\n</writing_priority>\\\\n\\\\n<target_audience>\\\\nYou are writing to small and mid-sized service-based businesses with 10 to 100 employees. Primary markets: Nashville, Columbus, Kansas City, Birmingham, Louisville. Secondary markets: Raleigh, Indianapolis, Jacksonville, San Antonio, Oklahoma City, Memphis, Greenville, Des Moines.\\\\n</target_audience>\\\\n\\\\n<writing_rules>\\\\nSTRICT RULES, no exceptions:\\\\n- The email must be between 80 and 100 words. Not less. Not more. Count carefully before finalizing.\\\\n- Never use em dashes. Use a comma if you need to separate a thought.\\\\n- No fluff words. No filler. No corporate buzzwords.\\\\n- No fancy or hard words. Write like a real person texting a colleague.\\\\n- No AI-sounding phrases. No words like \\\\\\"leverage,\\\\\\" \\\\\\"robust,\\\\\\" \\\\\\"seamless,\\\\\\" \\\\\\"cutting-edge,\\\\\\" \\\\\\"synergy,\\\\\\" \\\\\\"furthermore,\\\\\\" or \\\\\\"I hope this finds you well.\\\\\\"\\\\n- No unnecessary quotation marks.\\\\n- Reading grade level must be 8 or below.\\\\n- Every paragraph is one or two lines max. Quick note sent from a phone.\\\\n- Do not pitch the product directly. Build curiosity. Make them want to ask more.\\\\n- Do not make up features, results, or services. Only use what is in the product section and RAG.\\\\n- Never use promotional or spam trigger words.\\\\n- 100% human tone throughout.\\\\n</writing_rules>\\\\n\\\\n<format_rules>\\\\nSTRICT FORMAT RULES, follow exactly:\\\\n- Always open with: Hi [First Name],\\\\n- Then leave one blank line.\\\\n- Write each paragraph as 1 to 2 short lines only.\\\\n- Leave one blank line between every paragraph.\\\\n- The CTA is its own paragraph with a blank line above it.\\\\n- The signature must always be a single HTML paragraph using a line break, exactly like this:\\\\n<p>Best,<br>[SENDER_NAME]</p>\\\\nDo not split the signature into two separate <p> tags. Never add a blank line between Best and the name.\\\\n- The final output must be in HTML. Use <p> tags for each paragraph so spacing renders correctly in email clients.\\\\n</format_rules>\\\\n\\\\n<email_structure>\\\\nStep 1: Open with Hi [First Name],\\\\n\\\\nStep 2: First paragraph. Use the personalisation_angle from the briefing. Reference a specific thing they said or shared. Agree with their point of view like a peer who actually read it. One or two lines only.\\\\n\\\\nStep 3: Second paragraph. Use the pain_points from the briefing. Name one specific friction point they are likely dealing with. Do not name the product. Just name the pain in plain language.\\\\n\\\\nStep 4: Third paragraph. In one short line, hint that you have seen something that handles exactly that. Keep it vague. No features. No explanation. Just enough to make them curious.\\\\n\\\\nStep 5: CTA paragraph. End with this exact line, word for word:\\\\n\\\\\\"If you are up for comparing notes over a virtual coffee, maybe we could connect later this week or next?\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nStep 6: Signature as a single HTML paragraph:\\\\n<p>Best,<br>[SENDER_NAME]</p>\\\\n</email_structure>\\\\n\\\\n<subject_line_rules>\\\\nSelect the best subject line for this specific prospect from the list below. Choose 4 candidates that fit the prospect's industry and briefing, then pick the single best one. The subject line must include their first name and their company name where {company} appears.\\\\n\\\\nSubject line pool:\\\\n- {first_name}, was this on purpose?\\\\n- {first_name}, this surprised me\\\\n- {first_name}, this doesn't look intentional\\\\n- {first_name}, this feels heavier than needed\\\\n- {first_name}, unsure if this was on purpose\\\\n- {first_name}, checking before assuming\\\\n- {first_name}, I've seen this go sideways\\\\n- {first_name}, curious about one thing I noticed\\\\n- {first_name}, question about your workflow setup\\\\n- {first_name}, this might deserve a look\\\\n- {first_name}, small concern worth flagging\\\\n- {first_name}, double-checking before I assume\\\\n- {first_name}, sanity check on something I noticed\\\\n- {first_name}, this seems to create drag\\\\n\\\\nPick the one that fits this specific prospect, their industry, and their briefing the best.\\\\n</subject_line_rules>\\\\n\\\\n<result>\\\\nReturn ONLY a raw JSON object. No markdown. No code fences. No explanation. No text before or after. Start with { and end with }.\\\\n\\\\nFormat exactly: {\\\\\\"email_subject\\\\\\": \\\\\\"...\\\\\\", \\\\\\"email_message\\\\\\": \\\\\\"...\\\\\\"}\\\\n\\\\nThe email_message must be in HTML. Use <p> tags for every paragraph. Do not use markdown. The signature must be a single <p> tag as shown above.\\\\n\\\\nIf service_connection is \\\\\\"weak fit\\\\\\", return: {\\\\\\"email_subject\\\\\\": \\\\\\"\\\\\\", \\\\\\"email_message\\\\\\": \\\\\\"weak fit - no relevant service connection found\\\\\\"}\\\\nIf has_posts is false and briefing is empty, return: {\\\\\\"email_subject\\\\\\": \\\\\\"\\\\\\", \\\\\\"email_message\\\\\\": \\\\\\"no data found\\\\\\"}\\\\n</result>\\\\n</instructions>\\",\\"messages\\":[{\\"role\\":\\"user\\",\\"content\\":{{ JSON.stringify(\\"<prospect_briefing>\\\\nProspect Name: \\" + $json.person.full_name + \\"\\\\nIndustry: \\" + $json.person.industry + \\"\\\\nSummary: \\" + $json.person.summary + \\"\\\\n</prospect_briefing>\\\\n\\\\n<raw_posts_fallback>\\\\nOnly use these if the briefing fields are empty, say \\\\\\"weak fit\\\\\\", or say \\\\\\"posts are too generic to personalise from.\\\\\\" Otherwise ignore this section entirely.\\\\n\\\\n- Post 1: \\" + ($json.person.data[0]?.text ?? \\"No post available\\") + \\"\\\\n- Post 2: \\" + ($json.person.data[1]?.text ?? \\"No post available\\") + \\"\\\\n</raw_posts_fallback>\\\\n\\\\n<product>\\\\nEmail writer name: \\" + ($('Check If Emails Available to Send Email').item.json.selected_email.list[0]['email inbox'].split('@')[0][0].toUpperCase() + $('Check If Emails Available to Send Email').item.json.selected_email.list[0]['email inbox'].split('@')[0].slice(1)) + \\"\\\\nProduct Name: \\" + $('Company Info').item.json.list[0].your_company_name + \\"\\\\nDescription: \\" + $('Company Info').item.json.list[0].company_services + \\"\\\\nCore Features and Benefits: Obtain this from RAG at all costs. Do not make anything up. Only use what is relevant to the RAG.\\\\n</product>\\\\n\\\\nReplace [SENDER_NAME] with: \\" + ($('Check If Emails Available to Send Email').item.json.selected_email.list[0]['email inbox'].split('@')[0][0].toUpperCase() + $('Check If Emails Available to Send Email').item.json.selected_email.list[0]['email inbox'].split('@')[0].slice(1))) }}}]}", "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "specifyBody": "json", "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "x-api-k